From: abdulaziz <alanziabdulaziz4@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 05:30:51 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 08/15] server: give an opted-out slot a rollback snapshot
 budget of 0

At task launch, right after the drafting policy is fixed, set the slot's
sequence budget on the target memory: llama_n_rs_seq planes for a drafting
slot (today's K on every ubatch it takes part in), 0 for a slot whose request
sent "speculative.n_max": 0. Such a slot decodes with K = 1 -- one conv-state
copy, plane 0 only on the prompt ubatch, the generation ubatches and the
gathered transition ubatches -- node for node the graph the no-spec server
builds, so its residency is one S plane plus the prompt-end checkpoint that
both servers keep.

The refusal that a budget of 0 adds to llama_memory_seq_rm is unreachable
from the server for these slots: every partial tail removal it issues comes
from the verify loop (non-empty spec_draft only); the prompt-reuse path
resets or restores a checkpoint and then removes from cell.pos + 1, the
cache-reuse and context-shift ranges end at or before cell.pos, and rm_all
never enters the partial branch -- the same calls the FULL-type no-spec
server makes for every slot. A slot that inherits a pending rollback index
from an earlier drafting request reads a fully written plane (covered by
test-gdn-inplace). The MTP draft context on qwen35 holds a plain KV cache
and needs no call. LLAMA_SERVER_SPEC_MULTISLOT=0 keeps every budget at
n_rs_seq.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QrdPnP5KL449GsoWBZx52R
---
 tools/server/server-context.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tools/server/server-context.cpp b/tools/server/server-context.cpp
index 680359d..db0c0e8 100644
--- a/tools/server/server-context.cpp
+++ b/tools/server/server-context.cpp
@@ -1758,6 +1758,13 @@ private:
 
             slot.spec_enabled = slot.can_speculate() && (!spec_multislot || n_max_req != 0);
             slot.spec_n_max   = spec_multislot ? n_max_req : -1;
+
+            // rollback snapshot budget of the slot's sequence (recurrent memories; a no-op for the
+            // others): every plane for a drafting slot (K = n_rs_seq + 1, the unchanged graph), none
+            // for an opted-out slot (K = 1: plane 0 only, the graph the no-spec server builds). Set
+            // before the slot's first ubatch. The MTP draft context holds a plain KV cache, so the
+            // call goes to ctx_tgt only.
+            llama_memory_seq_rs_snapshots(llama_get_memory(ctx_tgt), slot.id, slot.spec_enabled ? llama_n_rs_seq(ctx_tgt) : 0);
         }
 
         slot.state = slot.task->is_child()
